// The demo world, `demo-gb [illustrative]` (docs/demo/WORLD.md): 93 historic counties of the
// United Kingdom, each its own node running the probe's four Appendix B roles
// (docs/probe/RULES.md) at its own instance, with no channels between them.
//
// Generated: do not edit. `rustyecon worldgen worlds/demo-gb --out tapes/demo-gb.ron`
// writes it from worlds/demo-gb/*.csv and the atlas data/atlas/gb.atlas.ron (ec2ee4100a483601),
// and the test `demo_tape_is_its_compilers_output` checks this file against the compiler.
//
// Illustrative: every entry's basis is Assumed("illustrative demo, ...") and the name
// carries [illustrative], so nothing from this tape may be scored or cited (R4, R5).
//
// Genesis puts every county at its own oracle point, as tapes/appb.ron is made (RULES §4):
// unit 1a (crates/oracle) at (rho, delta, J_b) = (0, 1, 1), solved at the county's
// per-tick instance, with every price divided by p/r so that the good costs 1 coin; the
// good desk holds one tick's Y of the good and the machine desk one tick's K of machine
// services, the good desk's human share is 1 - x*, and each actor's coin is its
// stationary balance under the dials. No agent reads the oracle at run time (R13).
//
// The history is 30078 dated SetParam steps on 1706 dates: each copies a schedule param
// county.<c>.<param>.<YYYY-MM> whose basis names the ramps of worlds/demo-gb/history.csv
// that moved it, stepped when the composed value has moved 0.01 in log (WORLD.md §4.3).
Tape(
    schema: 1,
    header: (
        name: "demo-gb [illustrative]",
        start: "1750-01-01",
